# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Project binaries (share the repo name, so the patterns above don't catch them)
/ai-agent-go-play
/agent

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
stderr.*

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Personal operator notes / scratch runbooks. These accumulate live tokens, chat ids, and
# deploy details; keep them out of the repo (see docs/planning/review-2026-08.md §1.8).
howtorun.txt
notes.txt
*.local.md
*.local.txt

# Per-deployment Fly config. The tracked deploy/fly/fly.*-agent.toml files are TEMPLATES
# (they carry "CHANGE ME"); a real app's name, region, and Telegram allowlist belong in
# an untracked copy.
deploy/fly/fly.local*.toml

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Agent runtime data: workspace-local memory + spaces (docs/adr/spaces.md)
.agent/
